WEBVTT

00:01:43.450 --> 00:01:44.580
Is it possible?

00:01:47.120 --> 00:01:48.540
Lie down, you two!

00:02:15.360 --> 00:02:18.450
Hey! Are you all right?

00:02:18.450 --> 00:02:20.160
What was that?

00:02:20.160 --> 00:02:21.990
Huh? Everyone's okay.

00:02:24.870 --> 00:02:26.870
Are you all right?

00:02:27.500 --> 00:02:29.580
Y-Yes!

00:02:29.580 --> 00:02:30.880
Who are you?

00:02:30.880 --> 00:02:34.210
Ah! That was quite close, wasn't it?

00:02:34.210 --> 00:02:37.220
Well, I'm glad. Everyone seems to be fine.

00:02:37.670 --> 00:02:39.180
Take it easy.

00:02:39.180 --> 00:02:41.220
That rat is mine.

00:02:41.220 --> 00:02:45.220
Kurotobi-san, weren't you
out with Tsuruume-san?

00:02:45.640 --> 00:02:47.480
I <i>did</i> go with her.

00:02:47.480 --> 00:02:50.980
She had something quite useful, so our errand went really fast.

00:02:51.690 --> 00:02:54.070
When we came back, you weren't there.

00:02:54.070 --> 00:02:57.400
And as I rushed here,
I saw a cohort of demons.

00:02:57.400 --> 00:02:59.990
What is this rat?

00:03:00.410 --> 00:03:02.490
This is a demon I raised specially.

00:03:02.490 --> 00:03:03.490
It's a type known as a fire rat.

00:03:04.200 --> 00:03:07.700
When I call him, he emerges and runs to me.

00:03:08.040 --> 00:03:10.620
Don't you know
"The Tale of the Bamboo Cutter"?

00:03:10.620 --> 00:03:14.420
The princess coaxed the Right Minister into getting her the fur of a fire rat.

00:03:14.420 --> 00:03:17.210
Its fur is very tough.

00:03:17.210 --> 00:03:21.220
Um, then... thank you very much.

00:03:22.140 --> 00:03:23.760
You're welcome.

00:03:23.760 --> 00:03:26.930
In fact, I didn't do anything special.

00:03:26.930 --> 00:03:31.690
I just controlled this demon well. That's all.

00:03:33.900 --> 00:03:36.190
People seem to be gathering
because of the commotion.

00:03:36.820 --> 00:03:40.320
You bastard. How dare you use fire!

00:03:42.280 --> 00:03:44.240
Oh, what?

00:03:44.240 --> 00:03:48.040
That explosion wasn't their doing.

00:03:48.040 --> 00:03:51.000
They seem to be heavily injured.

00:03:51.000 --> 00:03:54.210
It was probably a dust explosion.

00:03:54.210 --> 00:03:59.010
It's a natural phenomenon that can be caused by flour or dust.

00:03:59.010 --> 00:04:01.720
So the demons had nothing to do with it.

00:04:01.720 --> 00:04:03.930
Oh, I see.

00:04:03.930 --> 00:04:06.720
I don't know about that, so how do <i>you</i> know?

00:04:07.140 --> 00:04:13.020
Last month, I saw a news item about an accident like this, and I just remembered it.

00:04:13.020 --> 00:04:15.730
Although I didn't think
I'd experience it first-hand.

00:04:15.730 --> 00:04:18.520
Oh, was there an accident like that?

00:04:18.520 --> 00:04:22.070
You damned humans!

00:04:26.620 --> 00:04:28.490
What are you doing? Get back!

00:04:28.490 --> 00:04:30.750
What a brave swordsman.

00:04:30.750 --> 00:04:37.420
But I have to ask her something, so would you please wait?

00:04:37.420 --> 00:04:41.340
Didn't you do the same thing
at Naitou-Shinjuku?

00:04:41.340 --> 00:04:45.260
I think you killed a man named Genkichi by crushing him like this.

00:04:45.720 --> 00:04:47.550
You still stink.

00:04:47.550 --> 00:04:50.260
Your aura reeks of brutality.

00:04:51.770 --> 00:04:54.480
I don't know his name.
Why would I know his name?

00:04:54.480 --> 00:04:56.770
I killed him for revenge.

00:04:57.310 --> 00:05:02.030
He cut down my dear master and then put poison in him.

00:05:02.030 --> 00:05:06.660
First you worshiped him as a sacred tree,
then you suddenly and cruelly cut him down.

00:05:06.660 --> 00:05:10.160
That crime deserves death.

00:05:10.160 --> 00:05:12.370
The sacred tree was this demon's master.

00:05:13.040 --> 00:05:14.660
Then that trunk must be...

00:05:15.330 --> 00:05:17.000
Why did it happen?

00:05:17.000 --> 00:05:20.000
Oh, I see. I understand now.

00:05:20.000 --> 00:05:21.500
Please wait!

00:05:21.500 --> 00:05:24.760
Um, I don't think you have to kill her.

00:05:25.300 --> 00:05:28.800
Because she isn't really bad, right?

00:05:28.800 --> 00:05:33.020
Rather, a human who did bad things hurt something precious to her!

00:05:33.020 --> 00:05:34.520
Oh my, oh my.

00:05:34.520 --> 00:05:37.100
How kind you are, Rikugou-san.

00:05:37.100 --> 00:05:39.480
You sympathize with her, huh?

00:05:40.770 --> 00:05:43.990
Then what about this story?

00:05:44.740 --> 00:05:50.410
This demon killed Genkichi,
who had a daughter,

00:05:50.410 --> 00:05:52.990
his loving wife's posthumous child.

00:05:53.910 --> 00:05:55.250
As in a story you often hear,

00:05:55.790 --> 00:05:59.500
his daughter was sickly like her mother and suffered from serious illness.

00:06:00.000 --> 00:06:02.210
To make a lot of money quickly,

00:06:02.210 --> 00:06:06.010
he took a job transporting
dangerous medicines.

00:06:06.010 --> 00:06:08.220
I-I didn't know.

00:06:08.220 --> 00:06:10.140
You see the problem now.

00:06:10.140 --> 00:06:12.970
Same sinner, same crime.

00:06:12.970 --> 00:06:14.970
They're both to be pitied.

00:06:15.390 --> 00:06:19.690
If you look for reasons for sympathy,
you can find them anywhere.

00:06:20.610 --> 00:06:23.770
If reasons like that convince you
to sheathe your sword,

00:06:23.770 --> 00:06:25.940
it's easy to make a peaceful world.

00:06:25.940 --> 00:06:28.610
But matters don't turn out like that.

00:06:28.610 --> 00:06:30.530
Those who do harm should be exterminated.

00:06:30.530 --> 00:06:33.030
After all, that's the law of this world.

00:06:34.240 --> 00:06:35.540
I agree with that.

00:06:37.790 --> 00:06:40.830
Oh, here comes a very important person.

00:06:40.830 --> 00:06:42.340
Aren't you part of Amaza?

00:06:42.340 --> 00:06:44.550
You talk too much.

00:06:54.060 --> 00:06:56.020
Please, Buddha!

00:07:02.360 --> 00:07:06.530
If you used your own claws,
you'd find it easier to fight.

00:07:06.530 --> 00:07:12.160
Why don't you use the weapons you were given
when you were born, inugami?

00:07:12.530 --> 00:07:15.740
I see. That's why my master wants you.

00:07:15.740 --> 00:07:17.910
Inugami are very rare.

00:07:18.540 --> 00:07:21.290
If you call me by that name again,

00:07:21.290 --> 00:07:23.420
I'll kill you!

00:07:23.420 --> 00:07:24.670
Kuchiha!

00:07:24.670 --> 00:07:26.670
You don't have to cover for me anymore.

00:07:26.670 --> 00:07:29.130
H-Hey, what happened to Toki?

00:07:34.100 --> 00:07:37.640
I'm at a disadvantage against that thing.

00:07:39.100 --> 00:07:40.890
If Beni-chan were here...

00:07:41.230 --> 00:07:44.940
I know that I'm not really good
at these direct attacks.

00:07:44.940 --> 00:07:45.820
Toki?

00:07:45.820 --> 00:07:48.400
Idiot. What are you doing? Come back!

00:07:54.820 --> 00:07:57.120
Aren't you guys looking for this?

00:07:59.160 --> 00:08:01.870
Is that it? Is that my master's?

00:08:01.870 --> 00:08:05.080
I found it. I found it.

00:08:05.080 --> 00:08:08.550
Master is finally in my hand.

00:08:08.550 --> 00:08:11.340
Isn't that enough? Now take it and leave!

00:08:12.550 --> 00:08:16.140
I won't go back until I have avenged my master.

00:08:16.140 --> 00:08:17.510
I won't listen to you!

00:08:18.140 --> 00:08:21.100
I'm sad. I don't want to die.

00:08:21.100 --> 00:08:24.150
I'm sad. I don't want to lose you.

00:08:26.690 --> 00:08:31.030
I don't understand difficult things,
because I never thought about them.

00:08:31.900 --> 00:08:35.110
But... it can't be helped, right?

00:08:35.660 --> 00:08:37.120
This much I do<i> know.</i>

00:08:38.370 --> 00:08:39.290
Yes.

00:08:40.620 --> 00:08:44.370
I also didn't want to be alone.

00:08:45.920 --> 00:08:47.630
Hey, Imayou. Wait—

00:08:47.630 --> 00:08:50.500
Hey, brat! Sorry if this hits you.

00:09:06.600 --> 00:09:07.690
Bonten.

00:09:14.610 --> 00:09:17.660
Look, boss! It hit her right in the middle!

00:09:18.280 --> 00:09:21.040
Why are you taken in so easily?

00:09:21.040 --> 00:09:21.870
Do you want to die?

00:09:21.870 --> 00:09:24.370
Bonten, why are you here?

00:09:24.370 --> 00:09:26.670
Aren't you with Amaza?

00:09:26.670 --> 00:09:29.880
Why are you on their side instead of ours?

00:09:29.880 --> 00:09:33.010
Isn't Amaza our salvation?!

00:09:33.010 --> 00:09:34.130
Why?!

00:09:35.300 --> 00:09:38.640
That's just what you've been
ranting to yourselves.

00:09:38.640 --> 00:09:40.510
You might be mistaken.

00:09:40.510 --> 00:09:43.140
Yakou is an obstacle to me.

00:09:43.140 --> 00:09:46.310
Both the Princess and Yakou
are equal obstacles to me.

00:09:46.310 --> 00:09:48.690
I maintain harmony.

00:09:48.690 --> 00:09:51.150
Those who disrupt it are my enemies. That's all.

00:09:51.480 --> 00:09:55.650
You used Yakou's power to go too far.

00:09:55.650 --> 00:09:59.110
You've been reduced to being tools of Yakou.

00:09:59.110 --> 00:10:00.660
I don't need you anymore.

00:10:00.660 --> 00:10:04.910
On the other hand,
he's one of my most useful tools.

00:10:05.410 --> 00:10:07.290
If you lay a finger on him,
I won't forgive you.

00:10:07.290 --> 00:10:08.920
I'll take him back.

00:10:08.920 --> 00:10:12.550
Did you come here for this?

00:10:12.550 --> 00:10:16.920
You seem to be good at running errands.

00:10:17.510 --> 00:10:23.430
You can say what you want, but this demon has a special connection with me.

00:10:23.930 --> 00:10:25.930
If you lay a finger on her,
I won't forgive <i>you</i>.

00:10:25.930 --> 00:10:28.390
Tsuyukusa, you idiot.

00:10:28.390 --> 00:10:30.980
How shameful you look.

00:10:30.980 --> 00:10:33.940
Are you going to die for this fox?

00:10:33.940 --> 00:10:36.940
Shut up! If that brat is precious to you,

00:10:36.940 --> 00:10:38.950
why don't you take him with you right now?!

00:10:38.950 --> 00:10:40.660
If you're still going to block us,

00:10:41.120 --> 00:10:43.160
you're equally guilty!

00:10:45.910 --> 00:10:47.620
Damn it!

00:10:47.620 --> 00:10:49.710
What a fool.

00:10:49.710 --> 00:10:52.590
How dare you lift your hand against Bon?

00:10:52.590 --> 00:10:57.170
This idiot has gone crazy from Yakou's impurity, Utsubushi.

00:10:57.170 --> 00:10:59.930
He can't judge even the simplest thing.

00:10:59.930 --> 00:11:01.140
What a shame.

00:11:01.140 --> 00:11:04.140
Shut up. You're merely Bonten's sycophant.

00:11:04.640 --> 00:11:10.060
From the beginning, I never said that I'd just follow Bonten, like you did!

00:11:10.060 --> 00:11:12.150
What? Tsuyukusa, you...

00:11:12.150 --> 00:11:15.270
Geez, you're a disgrace.

00:11:15.270 --> 00:11:18.240
I never asked for flattery or followers.

00:11:18.240 --> 00:11:20.650
There's only one unwritten law.

00:11:20.650 --> 00:11:23.780
If you've forgotten it in your madness,
then you need to remember.

00:11:23.780 --> 00:11:29.660
I have always allowed dissent,
but I have never permitted resistance.

00:11:29.660 --> 00:11:32.580
Amaza has abandoned us!

00:11:32.580 --> 00:11:34.670
They're not really Amaza.

00:11:35.210 --> 00:11:36.130
Eat them.

00:11:36.130 --> 00:11:38.800
Eat the human-shaped things!

00:11:38.800 --> 00:11:40.670
Eat!

00:11:40.670 --> 00:11:43.050
Eat to the sound of Yakou's bell.

00:11:43.050 --> 00:11:44.390
Gouge out the guts.

00:11:44.390 --> 00:11:46.680
Suck out the blood!

00:11:47.310 --> 00:11:49.180
Why are you staring mindlessly?

00:11:52.520 --> 00:11:54.940
Are you all right, Rikugou-san?

00:11:56.820 --> 00:11:58.190
Shinonome's string!

00:11:58.190 --> 00:12:02.910
Before you worry about that,
you should see if your body is all right.

00:12:03.360 --> 00:12:05.870
I-I'm fine. Sorry.

00:12:05.870 --> 00:12:09.040
Never mind. More to the point,
we have to do something about that.

00:12:09.870 --> 00:12:13.000
The good thing is that the denizens of Amaza are quarreling among themselves.

00:12:13.000 --> 00:12:14.380
Hey, you guys...

00:12:14.750 --> 00:12:15.920
Heihachi-san?

00:12:17.340 --> 00:12:18.800
Hey, Utsubushi.

00:12:18.800 --> 00:12:21.050
I left him outside, like you said.

00:12:21.050 --> 00:12:25.760
It's not my responsibility if he climbed over the wall by himself.

00:12:25.760 --> 00:12:28.640
Heihachi, what are you doing here?

00:12:28.640 --> 00:12:31.560
He seems to have something to tell you.

00:12:31.560 --> 00:12:33.140
Listen to him, at least.

00:12:33.480 --> 00:12:35.650
Just when I thought I was rid of him.

00:12:35.650 --> 00:12:36.900
Are you an idiot?

00:12:36.900 --> 00:12:39.230
I don't have the time to talk
to you right now!

00:12:39.230 --> 00:12:40.400
Get out of here!

00:12:40.730 --> 00:12:43.240
I appreciate that you let me go,

00:12:43.240 --> 00:12:44.530
but listen to me.

00:12:46.490 --> 00:12:50.740
I'm truly sorry that humans cut down
the tree for their own convenience.

00:12:50.740 --> 00:12:55.170
But I don't want you to kill
the people in this store!

00:12:55.170 --> 00:12:58.750
They didn't act out of malice.

00:12:59.250 --> 00:13:02.920
An abandoned village was being redeveloped by official decree.

00:13:02.920 --> 00:13:06.260
The people there decided to sell some trees to wholesalers.

00:13:07.140 --> 00:13:09.260
So this is the tree.

00:13:09.260 --> 00:13:11.890
It really <i>is</i> a big camphor tree,

00:13:11.890 --> 00:13:14.690
but supposedly it's been hollowed out by disease.

00:13:14.690 --> 00:13:15.940
Hollowed out?

00:13:15.940 --> 00:13:18.810
Then it can't be used for building materials.

00:13:18.810 --> 00:13:21.610
All we can do is burn it as
a dedication or render it for oil.

00:13:21.610 --> 00:13:23.650
It may not be of use,
but it's still a sacred tree.

00:13:23.650 --> 00:13:26.490
We have to soothe the god's anger.

00:13:26.490 --> 00:13:29.780
But if we do that,
we'll go over budget.

00:13:31.580 --> 00:13:36.120
If no one is willing to take it,
allow me to do so.

00:13:36.120 --> 00:13:37.620
Nakamura-ya-san.

00:13:37.620 --> 00:13:40.880
I don't think you should take it.

00:13:40.880 --> 00:13:44.470
It's not a good fit for your trade.

00:13:44.470 --> 00:13:48.760
No, no. Camphor has a nice aroma.

00:13:49.090 --> 00:13:52.970
If I carve it properly, I can make
some good pipes from it.

00:13:53.390 --> 00:13:58.850
If we treat a big sacred camphor tree badly, we'll be cursed.

00:13:58.850 --> 00:14:03.530
Even if we cut it because of the official decree,
we have to thank it as it deserves.

00:14:03.530 --> 00:14:08.490
That way we can reward the tree
that has worked so long to protect us.

00:14:10.490 --> 00:14:15.120
He's a noble person to undertake such a money-losing task.

00:14:15.120 --> 00:14:18.500
Then, should we leave it to Nakamura-ya-san?

00:14:18.500 --> 00:14:20.500
Yes, we should.

00:14:20.500 --> 00:14:22.540
What an honest man he is.

00:14:22.960 --> 00:14:26.170
That's what it looked like to me,
even though I was just a bystander.

00:14:26.760 --> 00:14:29.260
I'll take it from here.

00:14:29.260 --> 00:14:35.720
It's an old story that was already
woven in heaven's net.

00:14:35.720 --> 00:14:41.520
That day, a man came to visit the carpenter.

00:14:41.810 --> 00:14:45.030
Is the rumor about the drug true, Genkichi?

00:14:45.030 --> 00:14:46.610
Yeah, it's true.

00:14:46.610 --> 00:14:48.740
A doctor who lives in
the neighborhood said it.

00:14:49.110 --> 00:14:53.280
I overheard it when I took
my daughter to see him.

00:14:53.280 --> 00:14:56.250
The doctor said that the drug he uses
when sewing up sword wounds

00:14:56.910 --> 00:15:00.750
has the same effect as
the prohibited drug opium.

00:15:00.750 --> 00:15:04.800
I see. Then you must go steal it.

00:15:04.800 --> 00:15:07.510
If you do that, I'll pay you
twice the normal price.

00:15:07.510 --> 00:15:10.590
But don't bring it straight to the store.

00:15:10.590 --> 00:15:13.510
The eyes of the people at the store
are sharper these days.

00:15:13.800 --> 00:15:17.220
No problem. I found a perfect container today.

00:15:17.220 --> 00:15:20.390
Just widen the opening,
and then drop the stuff inside.

00:15:21.350 --> 00:15:23.560
He deceived both the good and the bad,

00:15:23.560 --> 00:15:26.940
and the log and its contents were carried into the warehouse for storage.

00:15:26.940 --> 00:15:30.030
It was quite a wonderful idea.

00:15:30.030 --> 00:15:32.450
Unfortunately for the man,

00:15:32.450 --> 00:15:35.870
the fox demon missed the purification and didn't see her master's peaceful ascension.

00:15:35.870 --> 00:15:39.540
Had she known, she wouldn't have wreaked so much havoc.

00:15:39.540 --> 00:15:44.540
Was the master of Nakamura-ya burned so horribly because of that fox?

00:15:45.040 --> 00:15:48.260
It wouldn't be strange to think it was the divine tree's curse.

00:15:48.260 --> 00:15:52.510
No. The story of the fox and
the sacred tree is quite different.

00:15:53.010 --> 00:15:56.260
Tsuyukusa, I think you do understand.

00:15:56.720 --> 00:15:58.970
The sacred tree was purified properly,

00:15:59.470 --> 00:16:03.730
and the master of the tree went to heaven,

00:16:03.730 --> 00:16:07.020
leaving behind no hatred or curse.

00:16:07.360 --> 00:16:14.110
So you were taken in by a fretful fox
that really had nothing to avenge.

00:16:16.240 --> 00:16:18.200
You'd better stop this nonsense.

00:16:18.200 --> 00:16:22.290
That the owner of this store was injured demonstrates my master's hatred.

00:16:22.290 --> 00:16:26.750
No matter how much nonsense you spout,
this truth can never be changed.

00:16:26.750 --> 00:16:29.500
No. If what he's saying is true,

00:16:29.500 --> 00:16:32.130
I can understand now
why the warehouse seemed normal.

00:16:32.130 --> 00:16:36.760
The purification of the sacred tree worked
with miraculous efficiency.

00:16:37.260 --> 00:16:38.760
Then was it...

00:16:39.060 --> 00:16:40.270
Yes.

00:16:41.770 --> 00:16:45.770
By chance, the owner, who harbored suspicions about the head clerk,

00:16:45.770 --> 00:16:47.770
found the powder in the warehouse.

00:16:48.270 --> 00:16:51.070
When the panicked owner tried to take it out of the trunk,

00:16:51.070 --> 00:16:55.530
a lot of the powder fell
into the lantern at his feet.

00:16:55.530 --> 00:17:02.080
The powder caught fire and then burned the powder in the owner's hand.

00:17:02.790 --> 00:17:07.880
It spread to the camphor log, which burned easily,
and to the owner's clothes.

00:17:09.290 --> 00:17:12.050
I don't care if you call this
the god's punishment.

00:17:12.050 --> 00:17:14.930
But what you must do, Tsuyukusa,

00:17:14.930 --> 00:17:19.550
is return that demon, who's being
controlled by Yakou, to her senses.

00:17:19.550 --> 00:17:22.220
Shut up! What do you understand?

00:17:22.220 --> 00:17:24.560
You don't have the right to order me around!

00:17:26.980 --> 00:17:32.280
Bon, I think he did understand that.

00:17:32.280 --> 00:17:37.530
He just sympathized with the fox, who was going
to disappear still filled with regrets.

00:17:38.030 --> 00:17:41.540
I think he wanted to stop the fox.

00:17:42.620 --> 00:17:45.960
He probably became a bit emotional from overdoing things,

00:17:45.960 --> 00:17:50.040
and he ended up filled with Yakou's poison and dancing to his tune.

00:17:50.040 --> 00:17:53.050
The word idiot is saved especially
for someone like him.

00:17:54.010 --> 00:17:56.680
Tsuyukusa, sheathe your sword!

00:17:56.680 --> 00:18:02.180
Please. If matters continue this way,
you and the fox will not be treated kindly.

00:18:02.180 --> 00:18:06.810
If people and demons die in suffering...

00:18:06.810 --> 00:18:08.310
I don't want that to happen!

00:18:11.730 --> 00:18:13.980
Please. I beg you.

00:18:13.980 --> 00:18:16.320
Please help that fox!

00:18:17.650 --> 00:18:19.820
This is why I hate humans.

00:18:19.820 --> 00:18:22.580
They take everything, they notice nothing,

00:18:23.330 --> 00:18:25.580
and then they cry with the same face.

00:18:26.410 --> 00:18:27.870
So that's it, huh?

00:18:27.870 --> 00:18:29.080
That bell is...

00:18:31.000 --> 00:18:33.000
Boss! There are demons—

00:18:37.010 --> 00:18:39.260
You came here to pick up your failure.

00:18:40.220 --> 00:18:42.550
It wasn't a failure.

00:18:42.550 --> 00:18:46.480
They have seen a different
view of heaven's net.

00:18:47.060 --> 00:18:50.730
So I came here to pick them up before heaven destroys them.

00:18:52.730 --> 00:18:56.030
This could be an answer to my question.

00:18:56.030 --> 00:18:58.740
Isn't it regrettable for her
to end up dying this way?

00:18:58.740 --> 00:19:00.450
Yakou. She finally—

00:19:01.240 --> 00:19:02.740
How can you say that?

00:19:02.740 --> 00:19:08.460
It'd be better for her to die here than to be taken by you and treated as a specimen,

00:19:08.750 --> 00:19:11.960
or to lose her soul and be unable to reincarnate.

00:19:11.960 --> 00:19:15.130
Unfortunately, she's too conspicuous.

00:19:15.130 --> 00:19:17.090
Her anger is desperate.

00:19:17.090 --> 00:19:21.720
Even if she dies here,
she will never go to heaven.

00:19:22.550 --> 00:19:27.470
So I'll use her life to answer my question.

00:19:29.060 --> 00:19:31.060
Hey, stop that, Bonten!

00:19:31.060 --> 00:19:32.310
Why?

00:19:32.310 --> 00:19:33.480
"Why"?

00:19:34.110 --> 00:19:36.690
These are the consequences you chose.

00:19:38.190 --> 00:19:43.700
You told me that you had something to do
before you went back to your world.

00:19:43.700 --> 00:19:48.700
That is to lift Ginshu's curse, for Shinshu-chan.

00:19:48.700 --> 00:19:52.960
Because you wanted that,
I gave you the information.

00:19:53.630 --> 00:19:55.170
Because I wanted it?

00:19:55.170 --> 00:19:58.760
Now, you are the Blank Page.

00:19:58.760 --> 00:20:03.640
You're the only one besides Teiten
who can change the future of this world.

00:20:03.640 --> 00:20:04.930
Do you know what that means?

00:20:04.930 --> 00:20:09.470
If you don't want to make a choice,
then heaven's net won't change.

00:20:14.690 --> 00:20:16.650
Because I wanted it...

00:20:19.030 --> 00:20:22.990
Didn't Yakou also say that the results are not in heaven's net?

00:20:22.990 --> 00:20:28.370
Originally, the fox was supposed to curse and kill the people in the store.

00:20:28.830 --> 00:20:31.200
Humans who were supposed
to die were saved,

00:20:31.200 --> 00:20:33.620
those who were supposed
to be elsewhere came here,

00:20:33.620 --> 00:20:38.380
and a pitiful fox demon
was left with her regrets.

00:20:38.750 --> 00:20:43.510
Because you wished to save a human life
at the risk of a demon's,

00:20:43.510 --> 00:20:45.390
heaven's net has changed.

00:20:45.390 --> 00:20:46.470
Isn't that so?

00:20:47.800 --> 00:20:51.850
If you side with one of us,
naturally the other will lose out.

00:20:51.850 --> 00:20:55.400
Trying to depend on me while you still want to satisfy both...

00:20:55.400 --> 00:20:57.900
There are limits to selfishness.

00:20:57.900 --> 00:20:59.650
I didn't mean to do that.

00:20:59.650 --> 00:21:01.900
Then you must be satisfied with this.

00:21:02.650 --> 00:21:03.900
No.

00:21:06.410 --> 00:21:08.700
This is what you wanted.

00:21:08.700 --> 00:21:12.790
You should take responsibility
for this until the end.

00:21:15.540 --> 00:21:16.420
Rikugou-san.

00:21:16.880 --> 00:21:18.630
It's dangerous! Toki, get back!

00:21:19.090 --> 00:21:21.000
You idiot! What are you doing?!

00:21:21.000 --> 00:21:22.420
You'll be engulfed!

00:21:22.420 --> 00:21:24.130
Let me go, Heihachi.

00:21:24.760 --> 00:21:27.180
There's nothing you can do now!

00:21:27.180 --> 00:21:29.260
If you want to waste your life,
do it somewhere else!

00:21:29.800 --> 00:21:30.640
Shut up!

00:21:31.930 --> 00:21:35.060
Please. Could you be quiet for a while?
